# Private working material. These are excluded so a clone, a CI checkout or a
# fresh worktree cannot commit them: `.git/info/exclude` lives on one machine
# and does not travel, so it protected only the tree it was written in. One
# `git add -A` from anywhere else published the lot, permanently, which is not
# a hypothetical - a measurement directory reached a public pull request that
# way and its diff is still served. Names here are deliberate: naming a file is
# cheap, publishing its contents is not.
CLAUDE.md
CONTEXT.md
/docs/adr/
/docs/agents/
/.scratch/
/rigs/
/branding/
skills-lock.json
.claude/skills/
